# Testing Standards

## Types

| Kind | Suffix | Where |
|------|--------|-------|
| Unit | `.spec.ts` | next to code |
| Integration | `.integration.spec.ts` | next to code / infra |
| E2E | `.e2e.spec.ts` | `apps/api` or `test/e2e` |

Use **Vitest** everywhere. Prefer in-memory port fakes over mocks.

## Domain Unit Test

```typescript
// packages/domain/src/tenancy/tenant.spec.ts
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'
import { Tenant } from './tenant'
import { asTenantId } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/shared-kernel-types'

describe('Tenant', () => {
  it('emits TenantCreated on create', () => {
    const { tenant, events } = Tenant.create(asTenantId('…'), 'Acme')
    expect(tenant).toBeDefined()
    expect(events[0]?.type).toBe('TenantCreated')
  })

  it('rejects empty rename', () => {
    const { tenant } = Tenant.create(asTenantId('…'), 'Acme')
    expect(() => tenant.rename('  ')).toThrow()
  })
})
```

## Application Unit Test (in-memory ports)

```typescript
it('invites a member inside a unit of work', async () => {
  const memberships = new InMemoryMembershipRepository()
  const uow = new InMemoryUnitOfWork()
  const useCase = new InviteMemberUseCase(uow, authzFake, memberships)

  await useCase.execute({
    tenantId: asTenantId('t1'),
    email: 'a@example.com',
    roleIds: [asRoleId('r1')],
    actorUserId: asUserId('u1'),
  })

  expect(await memberships.count()).toBe(1)
})
```

## Coverage

Enforce ~90% on `packages/domain` only. Other layers: meaningful tests, no universal high threshold.

## Frontend

```typescript
render(<MemberCard member={membershipFixture} />)
expect(screen.getByText('active')).toBeInTheDocument()
```

Mock RTK hooks or use MSW for integration. Use contract types for fixtures.

## Commands

```bash
pnpm nx test domain
pnpm nx test application
pnpm nx affected -t test
```
